 "text": "Hey, nice to hear from you. How are you? The secret is never mixing your base with plain water. Use a tiny bit of lotions or creams as the solvent. Yes, in the summer. A light lotion or a thin cream as the base gives you a cool, almost denim finish. Try a light dusting of powdered clay mixed with a little lotion. For a warmer glow, add a few drops of rose water. Blending is the key. Start with a light shade for your under eyes, then build up the shadows and highlights. Blend them so there are no lines.",
